{:edb/db-before-t 2301 :edb/db-after-t 2302 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535614 50 #inst "2026-10-09T03:39:25.542Z" 13194139535614 true] [17592186357543 1100 "If $B$ is a $7\\times 12$ matrix that has $4$ **non-pivot** columns, then $\\text{dim(Null}(B))=$" 13194139535614 false] [17592186357543 1100 "Let $B$ be a matrix with $12$ columns and $4$ non-pivot columns, with enough rows for the $8$ required pivots ($m\\ge8$). What is $\\dim\\operatorname{Null}(B)$?\n\nHint: Each non-pivot column corresponds to a free variable. Check that the required pivot count can fit in the number of rows." 13194139535614 true] [17592186357543 1145 "Each non-pivot column corresponds to a free variable in $Bx=0$, so the null space has dimension equal to the number of non-pivot columns. There are $4$ such columns, hence $\\dim\\operatorname{Null}(B)=4$.\n\nThe pivot count is $12-4=8$, so $\\operatorname{rank}(B)=8$. Rank-nullity confirms $\\dim\\operatorname{Null}(B)=12-8=4$. A matrix with this rank must have at least $8$ rows. This is feasible for any row count $m\\ge8$; for example, put eight pivot columns and four zero columns in an $m\\times12$ matrix.\n\nThe original source specified a $7\\times12$ matrix with $4$ non-pivot columns. That would require $8$ pivots in only $7$ rows, contradicting $\\operatorname{rank}(B)\\le7$. No such original matrix exists. The corrected study question states the derived row requirement without choosing an arbitrary replacement row count. The original prompt, revealed answer $4$, worked solution and grade remain preserved as source evidence." 13194139535614 true] [17592186357543 1145 "We know that $\\text{dim(Null}(B))$ is the number of non-pivot columns in $B.$\n\nSince we are told that $B$ has $4$ non-pivot columns, we have \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(B))=4.\n$$" 13194139535614 false]] :edb/tempids {} :edb/committed false :edb/speculative true}
